identifier: PeelNStikThermal
name: Peel-N-Stik Thermal
description: |-
  Adds four radial peel-and-stik ablative heat shields (0.625 m to 3.75 m),
  scalable conformal decal coatings with four tile patterns, and four active
  heat sinks (CDH-4..7). The sinks pull interior and skin heat from every
  part in radius, store mild heat for free and bill the overflow to
  ElectricCharge. They brown out when power runs dry and blow like a
  sacrificial fuse at 1800 K, with an early warning in the part menu.
  CDH-7 projects a visible energy bubble, bills a flat EC/s per metre of
  radius and suppresses Firefly reentry FX inside the field. All sinks can
  be switched on/off in flight via the right-click menu or action groups.
  Firefly integration is optional; enhanced Firefly effects are still a
  work in progress.
author: Liam
$kref: '#/ckan/github/ehemaliger56-debug/PeelNStikThermal'
ksp_version: 1.12
license: restricted
tags:
  - parts
  - physics
  - plugin
  - graphics
depends:
  - name: ModuleManager
  - name: ConformalDecals
  - name: B9PartSwitch
  - name: ReStock
recommends:
  - name: Firefly
suggests:
  - name: SystemHeat
  - name: HeatControl
